MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You are correct. regionStats was not designed to look at individual probes. First, you need to do MAT normalisation on your arrays. This is implemented in aroma.affymetrix. Then, you extract the normalised values into a matrix. extractMatrix will do this. You can then create a model matrix and use limma. Doing your analysis is dubious, though, because the probes in a region of similar methylation can still have very different methylation estimates. I think you should do MAT smoothing, and stick to bigger regions. After all, your probes are 25 base pairs long, and your DNA fragments are around 500 bases long, so it's somewhat random to which closely spaced in the genome 25 base pair probe the DNA fragment binds to. If you had Illumina HumanMethylation450 arrays with the nucleotide resolution, then sure, but a tiling array doesn't make sense for measuring single probe locations. Smoothing and aggregating is the way to go.

